    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="233" column="1" str="/* ============================================================================= * Vector table * ============================================================================= * * Placed in its own section so the linker script can pin it to the * start of MRAM. The Cortex-M85 reads the initial MSP from offset 0 * and the reset vector from offset 4. */"/>
    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="242" column="1" str="/* Mach-O `section()` requires a `&quot;segment,section&quot;` form, but on the&#10; * host syntax-check / unit-test build we only need this array to&#10; * exist as a normal global -- the host never reads it from a fixed&#10; * vector address. So drop the section pinning on Apple hosts. */"/>
